---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/passive-fire.css"
import "aos/dist/aos.css";
const currentYear = new Date().getFullYear();
import { getSEO } from "../../utils/getSEO";
const seo = getSEO("passive-fire-service");
---

<Layout title={seo.title} description={seo.description} keywords={seo.keywords}>
    <section>
<div class="inner-banner">
  <div class="inner-banner-content">
    <h1>Services</h1>
    <p>Home / Services</p>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>
  <!-- ============================= -->
  <!-- 1) PLUMBING SERVICES (Left Image) -->
  <!-- ============================= -->
<section class="services-section">

  <div class="section-wrapper plumbing-wrapper" id="Passive Fire Services">

    <!-- IMAGE -->
    <div class="plumbing-image-box">
      <div class="dots"></div>
      <img src="/services/passive-fire4.png" class="section-img" alt="Passive fire service
" data-aos="fade-right">
    </div>

    <!-- TEXT -->
    <div class="plumbing-content">
      <h2   class="section-title section-title reveal-letters">Passive Fire Services
</h2>
      <p   class="section-text" data-aos="fade-up">
Our Passive Fire Services support building safety, regulatory compliance and asset management through the inspection, 
reporting, rectification and ongoing management of passive fire protection systems. Passive fire protection is a critical element of a 
building’s Essential Safety Measures (ESM), designed to contain fire and smoke, protect structural integrity and support safe evacuation.
 We deliver these services using industry-standard systems, including Vitals, to ensure accurate reporting, traceability and compliance.

      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
<section class="service-detail">
  <div class="image-container">
    <img src="/services/passive-fire3.jpg" alt="Passive fire servies" />
  </div>

  <div class="text-content">
    <h2   class="section-title section-title reveal-letters">What is Passive Fire Protection?

</h2>
    <p>
          Passive fire protection refers to fire safety measures that are built into the structure of a building and do not require activation to function. 
          These systems are designed to slow the spread of fire and smoke and maintain fire-resistance levels across fire-rated compartments. Passive fire 
          elements include fire-rated walls, floors and ceilings, fire doors, service penetrations and cavity barriers.

    </p>

    <h3>Our Passive Fire Services Include:</h3>

    <ul>
      <li>Passive fire audits and inspections of fire-rated building elements to assess condition and compliance</li>
      <li> Inspection and reporting using Vitals, providing structured, auditable and traceable compliance records</li>
      <li>Fire-stopping and penetration sealing to maintain fire-resistance ratings</li>
      <li> Inspection of fire-rated walls, floors, ceilings and compartmentation</li>
      <li>Fire door and fire-rated element condition assessments (where applicable)</li>
      <li>Defect identification and prioritised rectification recommendations</li>
      <li>Asset registers and ongoing compliance tracking managed through Vitals </li>
        <li>Vitals – Inspection, Reporting & Compliance</li>
    </ul>


     <h3>We utilise Vitals to manage passive fire inspections, audits and reporting. This system allows for:
</h3>

    <ul>
      <li>Digital inspection workflows aligned with passive fire requirements</li>
      <li>Photographic evidence and location-based defect tracking</li>
      <li>Clear identification of non-compliant items and required rectification works</li>
      <li>Centralised asset registers for passive fire elements</li>
      <li>Accurate records to support compliance obligations and building safety documentation
Using Vitals ensures consistency, transparency and reliable reporting across all passive fire assets.</li>
     
    </ul>

 <h3>Inspection & Reporting</h3>
   <p>
   Passive fire inspections are carried out in accordance with relevant Australian Standards and building compliance requirements.<br> 
   Each inspection produces a detailed Vitals report outlining:
   </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Items inspected</li>
      <li>Compliance status</li>
      <li>Identified defects or non-conformances</li>
      <li>Recommended corrective actions</li>
      <li>Supporting photographs and asset references</li>
    </ul>
   <p>Reports are suitable for compliance tracking, facility management and engagement with certifiers or consultants.</p>

   <h3>Why Passive Fire Compliance Matters</h3>
    <p>Passive fire systems form a critical part of a building’s Essential Safety Measures. Regular inspection and accurate reporting help ensure regulatory 
        compliance, protect occupants, reduce risk exposure and support certification and ongoing building management obligations.

    </p>
  </div>
</section>


</Layout>